From 2d1d91bcebc8fb645c2d0259b7efe4290e742234 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Wed, 20 May 2026 14:42:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] perf phase 11 patch 0165 -- Pixtone multi-source probe
 (486-campaign Bug 2 continuous-SFX-stutter probe)

486-campaign Bug 2 -- continuous SFX stutter on slow CPUs during
steady-state gameplay. flush-instr's #101 pre-flight grep refuted
the brief's headline candidate (pre-synthesize Pixtone SFX into
PCM): Pixtone::init() already pre-synthesizes each slot's chunk at
boot, and polar-star routes through the non-resampled Pixtone::play
path (p_arms.cpp:35-58) with no per-shot synthesis cost. So the
real cause is one of 5 hypotheses per docs/internal/PIXTONE-
MULTISOURCE-DESIGN.md sec.2 -- (A) per-callback mix CPU, (B)
track-state transition, (C) scheduler starvation, (D) IRQ jitter,
(E) re-diagnose -- and this patch is the probe that discriminates
them before we commit to another wrong-variable fix.

Probe-first iter (2-cell, DX2-66-only per [[486_iteration_workflow]]):
- PLAY0 baseline -- no SET, probe DISABLED, normal cell.
- PLAY1 SET SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_PIXTONE_PROBE=1 -- probe ENABLED;
  one [pixtone-multi] LOG_INFO line per 100-flip block lands in
  DEBUG.LOG with the hypothesis-discrimination signals.

After the iter, flush-instr's sec.20 findings name which hypothesis
matches the operator's reported stutter regime; the contingent v2
fix is authored against that.

Probe shape (one new audit line):
  [pixtone-multi block=N samples=N active min=X med=X p90=X max=X
   live=N stoptrack=N polarstar=N silent_irq=N]

Fields:
- block, samples -- block index + total samples collected this
  block (~140 expected at 30 fps Tier-2 over a 100-flip block, the
  audio-buffer-fill rate ~43 Hz drives sample rate).
- active min/med/p90/max -- g_pixtone_active_count distribution
  via 6 fixed buckets [0]/[1]/[2]/[3-5]/[6-10]/[11+] sampled in
  organyaStreamCallback at audio-buffer-fill cadence. Percentile
  values are bucket midpoints (0/1/2/4/8/12) via cumulative-count
  lookup -- coarse but sufficient at probe resolution. Captures
  SFX-storm bursts that collapse within one render frame.
- live -- instantaneous read of g_pixtone_active_count at the
  audit-flush boundary; ground-truth cross-check vs the histogram
  max bucket when SFX channels are mid-play at emit time.
- stoptrack delta -- block-over-block diff of
  g_pixtone_stoptrack_count (incremented at the 2 preempt-and-
  replay sites in Pixtone.cpp: play() at :454, playResampled() at
  :611). NOT incremented at the explicit-stop site (Pixtone::stop's
  MIX_StopTrack at :716) -- different mechanism per flush-instr's
  #104 sign-off. Channel-pressure indicator -- discriminates
  hypothesis B (track-state transition).
- polarstar delta -- block-over-block diff of
  g_pixtone_polar_star_count (combined counter for
  SND_POLAR_STAR_L1_2 (id 32) AND SND_POLAR_STAR_L3 (id 49);
  per-level disambiguation deferred to v2 if needed).
  Incremented in SoundManager::playSfx + playSfxResampled (where
  the SFX enum is in hand; Pixtone.cpp has only the slot-index
  abstraction). SFX-storm-rate indicator.
- silent_irq delta -- block-over-block diff of
  doskutsu_audio_silent_irq_count (SDL-side monotonic sibling of
  isr_consecutive_silent_irqs which resets on every non-silent
  IRQ; the monotonic version never resets). Read via extern from
  patches/SDL/0069. Scheduler-starvation + IRQ-jitter indicator.

Counter increments unconditional (volatile uint32_t, no atomics,
no fences; matches existing g_pixtone_active_count pattern). The
probe killswitch SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_PIXTONE_PROBE gates only the
LOG_INFO emit + the histogram bucket-inc -- both PLAY0 (probe off)
and PLAY1 (probe on) cells have valid counter snapshots
regardless of state.

Default-OFF byte-identical-at-rendered-frame to pre-0165:
- Counter incs are volatile uint32_t at file scope; no game-state
  mutation. ~10-50 Hz playSfx rate; negligible cost.
- The histogram-sample call site in organyaStreamCallback gates
  on pixtone_probe_active() and short-circuits when off (1 cached-
  int compare per audio buffer fill, ~43 Hz).
- The audit body in _maybe_flush_pixtone_multi_audit gates on
  pixtone_probe_active(); when off, resets the histogram (so a
  mid-run SET starts clean) and returns without emit.
- pixtone_probe_active itself emits one LOG_INFO banner line on
  first call regardless of state (banner-only-no-state-change
  pattern, matches 0162-v2 / 0163 / 0164).

Killswitch: SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_PIXTONE_PROBE, strict-"1" opt-in,
default OFF. Same hygiene as nxengine/0162-v2 + 0163 + 0164.
Sentinel-cached on first pixtone_probe_active() call -- single
_strict_truthy_env (std::getenv-backed) then cached int; banner
emit "pixtone multi-source probe: ENABLED (opt-in)" /
"pixtone multi-source probe: DISABLED (default)" on the decision.

Cross-TU layout (mirrors the existing [audio-block] reader pattern):
- Pixtone.h: +2 extern decls (g_pixtone_stoptrack_count +
  g_pixtone_polar_star_count) next to existing
  g_pixtone_active_count.
- Pixtone.cpp: +2 file-scope counter defs in the existing
  extern "C" {} block; +2 inc sites (one at the preempt path in
  play() at :454, one at the resampled preempt path in
  playResampled() at :611).
- SoundManager.cpp: +1 cmp+inc in playSfx (after the Pixtone
  dispatch); +1 cmp+inc in playSfxResampled (defensive mirror for
  any future mod / patch routing polar-star resampled). Both
  count toward g_pixtone_polar_star_count.
- Organya.cpp: +1 NXE::Diag::SamplePixtoneActiveBucket call at the
  top of organyaStreamCallback (after AudioMixerTimer, before the
  additional_amount<=0 fast-skip -- the sampler runs even on
  zero-work callback wakeups since those still represent audio-
  thread cadence ticks worth measuring).
- diagnostic_timers.h: +1 forward-decl for
  NXE::Diag::SamplePixtoneActiveBucket (decl in NXE::Diag
  namespace; defn at file-scope-after-both-namespace-closes in
  Renderer.cpp per the W20B/W22A wrapper pattern).
- Renderer.cpp: +5 extern decls in the existing extern "C" {}
